cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Machine-checked proofs of relations in physical geodesy"
message: "If you use this material, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Arana
    given-names: Daniel
    affiliation: "Universidade Federal do Paraná"
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 formalisation, over the mathlib library, of relations in physical
  geodesy: the geoid-quasigeoid separation as an algebraic identity rather than two
  independent routes; the rigid limit of the gravimetric and tilt factors, together
  with the vanishing of the displacement factors in the asymptotic regime; the
  invariance of the asymptotic Boussinesq ratio with respect to gravity and shear
  modulus; the implication from Hormander's uniqueness condition to the
  Lions-Sznitman well-posedness condition, with an explicit counterexample to the
  converse; and the nullity of the degree-zero load Love number as a consequence of
  mass conservation. Every theorem prints its axiom dependencies during the build,
  and none depends on an axiom outside the three standard ones. No observational
  data are used.
keywords:
  - physical geodesy
  - formal verification
  - interactive theorem proving
  - Lean 4
  - mathlib
  - height systems
  - load Love numbers
  - geodetic boundary value problem
license: Apache-2.0
